{"created": "2026-10-13T04:16:07.006521+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-13T04:16:08.923373+00:00", "id": 23331295, "conceptrecid": "23331294", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23331295", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23331294", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331295", "metadata": {"title": "An elementary counterexample to a Nullstellensatz for finite-type link invariants", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23331295", "publication_date": "2026-10-12", "description": "<p>We give a principal-ideal counterexample to the arbitrary-ideal actual-link Nullstellensatz in the ordinary uncompleted complex algebra of all finite-order finite-type link invariants. With g the sum of squared pairwise linking numbers and f=g(4g-1), the nonempty common zero set is the algebraically split links, but g does not lie in the radical of fV. A character on the entire algebra is obtained by formal evaluation of the standard twist-restriction polynomial at one half. The result applies for every fixed component count m at least two and for all finite-component links; the source's separate indexed linking-number ideal in the labelled theory is not decided.</p><p>This is an elementary application of older polynomiality, explicitly credited to Stanford-Trapp, Eisermann and Stoimenow. A bounded primary-source audit found no explicit equivalent earlier counterexample in the inspected bodies, without claiming historical firstness, a new polynomiality method, or guaranteed novelty. The included audit discloses uninspected final-version/body limits. The deposit includes the self-contained research note, LaTeX source and exact-rational verification materials.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in developing, drafting, auditing and adversarially checking the result. This preprint is unrefereed and has not undergone conventional human peer review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["finite-type invariants", "Vassiliev invariants", "link invariants", "Hilbert Nullstellensatz", "linking numbers", "radical ideals", "twist sequences"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/177", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1142/S0219199710003944", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://msp.org/gtm/2002/04/gtm-2002-04-024s.pdf", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23331294"}}]}, "notes": "Research note recording an explicit counterexample to the literal arbitrary-ideal formulation of Bar-Natan's Problem2.27. Ordinary uncompleted characteristic-zero algebra; no positive-characteristic, homogeneous-ideal, completed-algebra or labelled linking-number-generated-ideal resolution is claimed. AI-assisted; not conventionally human peer reviewed."}, "title": "An elementary counterexample to a Nullstellensatz for finite-type link invariants", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331295", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331295?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331295", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331295", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23331295", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331294", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331294", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23331294", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23331294", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295:nullstellensatz.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295:nullstellensatz.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295:nullstellensatz.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295:nullstellensatz.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295:nullstellensatz.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23331295:nullstellensatz.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23331295/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23331295/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-13T04:16:08.923373+00:00", "recid": "23331295", "revision": 3, "files": [{"id": "9c37ac12-59db-4444-8227-0c94203cbcdb", "key": "